, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[6]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[7]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[7]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[7]},{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[8]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[8]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[8]},{"id":"jesus_905","name":"Jesus","also":"Immanuel, Emmanuel, Messiah, Shiloh, Christ, Jesus Christ, Messias","summary":"Anointed, the Greek translation of the Hebrew word rendered “Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen